---
import MacDesktop from "../layouts/MacDesktop.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/macos/PageHeader.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../site";
---

<MacDesktop title="Projects">
	<div class="flex h-full max-h-full flex-col gap-2 p-4 sm:p-8">
		<PageHeader title="Projects" />

		<article class="prose max-w-full">
			<ul class="divide-y divide-dotted divide-black">
				<li>
					<a
						class="underline"
						href="https://github.com/ethanl21/calsafe"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">CalSafe</a
					>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<i
								class="icon-[logos--nextjs-icon] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"
							>
							</i>Full-stack crash analytics dashboard in Next.js — 629,000+
							accident records, filterable by location, severity, and date
						</li>
						<li>
							Revamped Jul 2026: Django REST API on Heroku → <i
								class="icon-[logos--nextjs-icon] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Next.js API routes with <i
								class="icon-[fa7-solid--database] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Turso; upgraded Next.js, React,
							shadcn/ui, and <i
								class="icon-[logos--tailwindcss-icon] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Tailwind CSS on <i
								class="icon-[logos--vercel-icon] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Vercel
						</li>
						<li>
							<i
								class="icon-[logos--docker-icon] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Docker Compose self-host for testing
							(Portainer, NGINX, Cloudflare DNS); scheduled data import in
							progress
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a
						class="underline"
						href="https://github.com/cuebitt/patchwork"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Patchwork</a
					>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<i
								class="icon-[logos--java] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Client-side Minecraft mod adding a trowel
							item for placing random blocks from your inventory
						</li>
						<li>
							Published to Modrinth via <i
								class="icon-[fa7-brands--github] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>GitHub Actions (109+ downloads); works on
							any server, no server-side install needed
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a
						class="underline"
						href="https://github.com/cuebitt/hypercutter"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">hypercutter</a
					>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<i
								class="icon-[logos--rust] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>CLI + reusable Rust crate that extracts
							sprite and tileset assets from GBA Pokémon ROMs
						</li>
						<li>
							Reverse-engineered an undocumented binary format; rewrote from
							<i
								class="icon-[logos--python] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Python to Rust — no runtime dependency,
							faster execution
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a
						class="underline"
						href="https://github.com/cuebitt/bluesoil"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">bluesoil</a
					>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<i
								class="icon-[logos--react] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Drag-and-drop UI builder in React for
							Basalt 2.5 (CC: Tweaked)
						</li>
						<li>Serializes the visual tree to JSON, XML, and Lua</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a
						class="underline"
						href="https://github.com/ethanl21/setup-quickjs-ng"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">setup-quickjs-ng</a
					>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<i
								class="icon-[fa7-brands--github] align-middle leading-none"
								aria-hidden="true"></i>Reusable GitHub Action that sets up
							quickjs-ng for later CI steps
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				For more information, please visit my{" "}
				<a
					class="underline"
					href={GITHUB_URL}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
				>
				page.
			</p>
		</article>
	</div>
</MacDesktop>
